    <string name="enable_screen_share">Allow watching this screen</string>
    <string name="enable_screen_share_info">Lets a signed-in user watch this computer's screen live from the web interface, under &quot;Remote screen&quot; in the file browser menu.\n\nThe screen is captured only while somebody is actually watching, and streamed as H.264 video over the same connection - and the same encryption - as the rest of the server. Nothing is recorded on this machine; the viewer can save what they see to a file of their own.\n\nWhen authorization is enabled, a user needs the &quot;View screen&quot; permission before they can watch - grant it per user or per role on the users screen. With authorization switched off, anyone who can reach the server can watch.\n\nThe primary monitor is shared.</string>
    <string name="enable_remote_control">Allow controlling this computer</string>
    <string name="enable_remote_control_info">Lets a viewer of the shared screen also drive this computer: move the pointer, click, scroll and type.

When authorization is on, an account needs the "Control screen" permission on top of "View screen". When authorization is off, anyone who can reach this server can drive this computer.

Only one viewer controls the machine at a time; the others are told it is busy until whoever is using it stops. Keyboard forwarding has to be switched on in the browser page and released with a button there, because while it is on the page sends shortcuts to this computer instead of acting on them itself.</string>

